Finding: {"title":"Fee-definition rows summing above their parent fee item silently over-allocate to certificates without correction","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"Certificate cost breakdown","files":["src/lib/training-plan-certificate-cost.ts"],"detail":"In buildTrainingPlanCertificateCosts (lines 128-147), when a fee item has definitions (per-certificate splits), the code sums definitionTotalCents and only corrects for itemAmountCents > definitionTotalCents (excess routed to unallocatedFeeCents). There is no symmetric handling for definitionTotalCents > itemAmountCents — if per-certificate definition amounts sum to more than the parent fee item's total, each certificate still receives its full definition amount with no scaling or flag.","impact":"allocatedFeeCents (and each certificate's feeAmount/totalAmount) can overstate the true fee total relative to itemAmountCents, and plannedTotal will not reconcile against the actual fee item amounts. This surfaces as an inflated per-certificate quote total with no integrity check catching it.","recommendation":"When definitionTotalCents > itemAmountCents, either proportionally scale each definition's contribution down to match itemAmountCents, or treat it as a data-integrity error and route the excess to unallocatedFeeCents / log a warning rather than silently over-allocating.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

